  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential repurposing of Isoniazid for Pulmonary Tuberculosis, mediated through off-label use of related compounds. Isoniazid is linked to Recurrent Pneumonia (disease) via off-label use, which in turn is associated with Ethionamide and Rifampicin, both of which have established indications for Pulmonary Tuberculosis. This creates a chain of off-label use that indirectly links Isoniazid to the disease, though the direct relationship remains unestablished. The evidence highlights a possible pathway where Isoniazid's off-label use of related drugs may contribute to the treatment of Pulmonary Tuberculosis, though further validation is needed to confirm the exact mechanism and clinical relevance.",
